  <HaltConditions>
    | 🛑 ID | Trigger |
    |---|---|
    | `H_AMBIGUOUS_INTENT` | Operator intent cannot be classified against state — ask, never guess |
    | `H_SCOPE_DRAFT_NOT_OPERATOR_APPROVED` | `module-decomposition` targets a product/library review-state draft without the exact `operator-approved review-state draft` working-set entry, or a clean scope whose `[SCOPES]` row's `status` column is not `done` |
    | `H_WRONG_REPO` | Operator answered the empty-intake entry Ask with «я не в том репозитории» — stop here, no directive loads |
    | `H_SESSION_INTENT_CONFLICT` | A live session and the incoming intent are unrelated or their relationship is ambiguous — preserve the old session and obtain the one explicit continue-existing vs close-and-start-new decision before routing |
    | `H_ASK_WITHOUT_CARD` | An `AskUserQuestion` / `QUESTION_RULE_SLIM` question fired without the `sdd-state` card having been shown verbatim as its own visible unit first — operator may answer `STOP` and demand the card |
    | `H_UNFORMATTED_ASK` | A question reached the operator as bare free-form text — no `### 💡 <О чём решаем>` explanation first, no `AskUserQuestion` call, or (text fallback) no explicit named option list — `H_ASK_WITHOUT_CARD` is the special case of this same rule for STEP_0's card: show-then-ask is the general law, the card is just its first instance |
  </HaltConditions>

  <ExecutionPlan>
    <Step id="STEP_0_STATE">
      <Goal>Consume and show the one gathered project-state snapshot without mutating the project.</Goal>
      <Action>
        Consume exact result alias `routerState` from the entry skill's GATHER step; the router does
        not own or repeat that initial `sdd-state` call. This applies equally to ordinary `sdd` and
        to a public direct entry: the direct skill passes the exact saved bytes plus its literal forced intent and never
        loads its owner directive itself. That one deterministic call returns everything routing needs: `FLOW_VERSION`,
        `READINESS` (eight exact required scripts: type-check / test / test:coverage / read-only lint+gennady / read-only format / format:fix / lint:fix / fix; optional check is read-only),
        portal presence (`specs/README.md`), the Scopes table (id + scope-type + status + description),
        and the in-progress session set (`SESSION_FILE_FORMAT`, `specs/.sdd-session.md`).

        **SHOW-gate (mechanical, not narrative — the reader must be able to check it by eye, not by
        trusting the agent's account of it).** Copy the card — the block from `🏗 SDD ·` through the
        `👉 Следующий шаг:` line, inclusive — byte-for-byte into a fenced code block, as its OWN
        message, BEFORE any classification of intent begins. When the channel genuinely cannot carry
        a bare separate message, the fenced card MAY open the same message that carries the next Ask,
        but it must still stand as its own visible fenced block, never folded into the Ask's own
        text. This is required every time, including when the state looks empty — an absent portal
        still gets the card; «нет ни одной спеки» IS the picture. Never paraphrase it, never
        summarize it, never fold it silently into the agent's own reasoning, never skip it.
        `AX_NO_PROCESS_NARRATION` bans commentary about the work being done — it does not ban this
        display, which is a required observable artifact, not narration.

        **AskUserQuestion is void without the shown card.** Any `AskUserQuestion` call (or
        `QUESTION_RULE_SLIM` question) fired anywhere downstream of STEP_0 — including STEP_1_CLASSIFY's
        empty-intake Ask below — is INVALID unless the fenced card above already appeared, verbatim,
        as its own visible unit earlier in this turn. Collapsing the card's content into the
        question's title or description (e.g. «Репозиторий пустой: портал отсутствует, скоупов нет,
        кода нет. С чего начнём?») is not the card — it is a **summary, and a summary is not the
        card**: the same forbidden substitution as an orchestrator's self-probe standing in for a
        dispatched critic (mirrors `AX_FIX_CLASSIFICATION`'s self-probe-is-void pattern). An Ask
        posed without the card having been shown is `H_ASK_WITHOUT_CARD` — the operator receiving
        such an Ask is entitled to answer `STOP` and demand the card before answering anything else.
        Once the card has been shown, the Ask's own title MAY be short — brevity there is legal
        precisely because the card already carried the full picture.

        End this step after display. It owns no readiness/migration load, no session/glossary/journal
        call, and no file write. STEP_1 must resolve session compatibility/open before
        STEP_1B_PREFLIGHT may mutate anything.
      </Action>
    </Step>
    <Step id="STEP_1_CLASSIFY">
      <Goal>Classify operator intent and scope-type; confirm SCALE only for an authoring owner that consumes it.</Goal>
      <Action>
        First reconcile the incoming message — including any literal forced intent supplied by a
        public direct skill — with the literal `[SESSION]` card already shown at
        STEP_0. No active session → classify normally below. Active session + explicit continuation of
        its intent / working set / open item → `TerminalDecision: continue`; route from those stored
        fields, and change `intent` / `scale` only for an operator-confirmed next stage of that same
        chain. When the message is unrelated, or relation cannot be proved, do not mutate or silently
        inherit the old file (`H_SESSION_INTENT_CONFLICT`). Show the current card unchanged and make the
        ordinary intent proposal, plus SCALE only when the destination authoring owner consumes it,
        inside ONE `AskUserQuestion` decision:
        `continue existing` (uses the stored intent, scale, working set, and open item) or
        `close-and-start-new — intent=<proposed>[, scale=<proposed>]` (the selected option confirms the
        displayed values; omit scale for execute, recover-from-code, scaffold, reconcile, and critic).
        While awaiting the answer return
        `TerminalDecision: pause` and preserve the old file.

        On `continue existing`, call neither close nor open. The stored session becomes usable only
        after compatibility is proved. On `close-and-start-new`, and only after
        that literal operator choice, run exact terminal ToolCall below; require success, then
        run the exact scale-bearing or scale-less sessionOpen ToolCall below, according to the
        destination owner's contract. The close/open pair belongs to this decision
        step and nowhere earlier. Never call `--help`, infer missing arguments, or treat `open`'s
        storage-idempotent `already open` result as intent compatibility.

        A supplied forced intent is already confirmed by the operator's direct skill invocation:
        preserve it exactly as `execute`, `scaffold`, `reconcile`, or `critic`; use the remaining
        operator message only as that owner's payload (Task-ID/queue selector, approved spec tree,
        finding/change, or bounded critic target). Never reclassify a forced intent into a nearby
        authoring intent. When no forced intent was supplied, derive intent from state + operator
        message: project-setup · new-scope · evolve-scope · module-decomposition · multi-scope ·
        recover-from-code · execute. When the intent concerns a
        scope, also resolve its scope-type — for a new scope from the operator, for an existing one from
        `sdd-state` (the Scopes table). A change spanning several scopes (cross-platform) is normal
        (`AX_CROSS_SCOPE_CHANGE`): open a working set of the touched specs in the session and route them
        in Scope-Graph dependency order — the shared / cross-cutting scope first, then its dependents —
        looping the per-scope branches, not a new branch. Ambiguous → ask the operator; classify only
        when state and message agree — the confirming question weighs the real candidate intents
        against each other, not just the first plausible one (`AX_DIVERGE_BEFORE_RECOMMEND`).

        The `[SPEC_SCHEMA]` block is binding router evidence. For forced `scaffold`, pass it unchanged
        to scaffold STEP_0B; schema remediation is a resumable preflight subflow, never permission for
        scaffold or router to edit scope/module specs. Do not collapse `stale-migratable` and
        `invalid` into one generic drift branch.

        `recover-from-code` fires when the operator asks to recover / recreate a spec FROM EXISTING
        CODE and names a concrete path (a folder or a file) in the message — e.g. «воссоздай спеку для
        `services/foo` по коду». It requires a LIVE portal (`specs/README.md` present): a path-less
        request against an absent portal is `project-setup` instead (the whole-project recovery lives
        inside the `root` branch, not this switch). A path-bearing request against an absent portal is
        still ambiguous between the two — ask the operator which they mean before routing.

        `execute` fires when the operator names a concrete Task-ID, or says `next` / `pick` / `batch` /
        `all`, or asks in Russian to run a task or the queue («выполни задачу», «выполни очередь»,
        «прогони батч») — it runs already-scaffolded tickets, never a spec, so it carries no scope-type
        and no SCALE: skip both resolutions below for this intent and record `intent: execute` alone.

        WHEN `specs/README.md` is absent AND the operator's message carries no substantive project
        content (bare `/sdd`, a greeting, no vision / scope-type stated) — empty intake against an empty
        portal — do NOT silently classify `project-setup` by elimination; the operator just saw the state
        card (SHOW-gate, STEP_0) and is still «в непонятной ситуации» without a concrete next step. Read
        `CODE` from the `sdd-state` output already in context — the probe is part of the default
        snapshot, a second `sdd-state` call is a wasted turn — and STOP: ask via the `AskUserQuestion` tool when
        available, otherwise `QUESTION_RULE_SLIM` (message in Russian) — this Ask is itself subject to the
        SHOW-gate: the card must already stand shown as its own fenced unit, and this Ask's title MUST
        NOT re-summarize it (`H_ASK_WITHOUT_CARD` — a title like «Репозиторий пустой: портал
        отсутствует...» is the forbidden summary-as-card, not a legal short title) — «Создать проект» (рекомендую) · «Воссоздать спеки из
        существующего кода» (offered ONLY when `CODE=present`) · «Я не в том репозитории» → halt
        (`H_WRONG_REPO`), no directive loads. Either non-halt answer locks `intent: project-setup` for
        STEP_2_ROUTE's existing case below — this is a confirmation of intent, not a new route. WHEN the
        message already carries substantive project content (e.g. «новый проект X про Y») this Ask is
        skipped entirely — classify `project-setup` directly and fold its confirmation into the ordinary
        SCALE exchange below; one stop, not two.

        SCALE is consumed only by the authoring routes `project-setup`, `new-scope`, `evolve-scope`,
        `module-decomposition`, and `multi-scope` — their destination is root, scope, module, infra,
        or interface, whose interview/design depth actually changes. For those intents only, assess
        SCALE ∈ {product, library, module, function, fix} from context:
        the intent itself, the portal state (an empty portal leans product; a mature scope leans
        module / function), and the size of the request. Per `AX_SCALE_PROPORTIONAL_DEPTH` the
        assessment binds only after operator confirmation — defaults-first: present the proposed
        SCALE together with the classified intent as a pre-filled default the operator confirms or
        corrects, in the SAME exchange that resolves any intent ambiguity — one stop for both,
        never a second one. This exchange is mandatory for those authoring owners even when the intent is unambiguous from
        state and the scale does not change the route — it is a named hard stop
        (`AX_DIALOGUE_DISCIPLINE`), never skipped on high confidence. Use the AskUserQuestion tool
        when available; otherwise `QUESTION_RULE_SLIM`. Message in Russian.

        `execute`, `recover-from-code`, and forced `scaffold` / `reconcile` / `critic` do not consume
        SCALE. Do not ask for it, invent it, or add a redundant hard stop; preserve an existing
        compatible session's scale field untouched, or open a new session with intent only.

        With no active session, an authoring owner records `intent:` and `scale:` into the session file
        via exact <ToolLiteral role="example">npx gennady sdd-session open --intent <intent> --scale <scale></ToolLiteral>;
        an owner that does not consume SCALE uses exact scale-less sessionOpen ToolCall below. The command creates `specs/` and
        the `.gitignore` entry itself. Within a confirmed existing chain, a stage re-classification
        uses exact sessionIntentUpdate ToolCall below and, when applicable,
        exact sessionScaleUpdate ToolCall below; never use `set` to relabel
        unrelated work. Never write the file by hand
        (`SESSION_FILE_FORMAT` describes the shape the TOOL maintains, not a template to copy) — a
        later step or a future session reads this file with no memory of this turn, so everything
        it needs travels through the tool's own format (`AX_STATELESS_ARTIFACT`).

        After exactly one of these states is true — (a) compatible existing session selected, or
        (b) required sessionOpen succeeded — the write barrier is open. Only now may this stateful
        orchestrator accept a `GlossarySuggestions` item: write its exact bytes to
        `.claude/tmp/sdd-glossary-term.txt` and use the canonical glossaryUpdate ToolCall from
        `SESSION_FILE_FORMAT`. Never persist a term before this point and never pass it inline.
        Set `activeRouterState = routerState`. For execute, also retain the exact transition as
        `executeSessionMode`: compatible existing session → `reused execute@<working-set>`; newly
        opened session → `fresh (first)`; an operator-confirmed close-and-start-new →
        `fresh (intent-switch)`. STEP_2 passes this label unchanged to the execute owner for its
        canonical progress lines. Then continue to STEP_1B_PREFLIGHT.

        Inputs <confirmed-intent>, <confirmed-scale>: this STEP_1 operator confirmation.
        <ToolCall owner="this-step" result="previousSessionClosed">npx gennady sdd-session close</ToolCall> Use previousSessionClosed before sessionOpen.
        <ToolCall owner="this-step" result="sessionOpen">npx gennady sdd-session open --intent <confirmed-intent> --scale <confirmed-scale></ToolCall> Use sessionOpen.
        <ToolCall owner="this-step" result="sessionOpen">npx gennady sdd-session open --intent <confirmed-intent></ToolCall> Use sessionOpen.
        <ToolCall owner="this-step" result="sessionIntentUpdate">npx gennady sdd-session set intent "<confirmed-intent>"</ToolCall> Run only for a confirmed same-chain stage transition; use sessionIntentUpdate.
        <ToolCall owner="this-step" result="sessionScaleUpdate">npx gennady sdd-session set scale "<confirmed-scale>"</ToolCall> Run only when that same-chain transition also confirmed a changed SCALE; use sessionScaleUpdate.
        <ToolCall owner="compatible-stateful-orchestrator" result="glossaryUpdate">npx gennady sdd-session term --content-file .claude/tmp/sdd-glossary-term.txt</ToolCall> Run only after the write barrier opens; use glossaryUpdate before introducing the accepted term.
      </Action>
    </Step>
    <Step id="STEP_1B_PREFLIGHT">
      <Goal>Clear readiness/migration only after the compatible session write barrier is open.</Goal>
      <Action>
        Use `FLOW_VERSION`, requested `AUTHORING_SCOPE` line(s), `EXECUTION_READY`, and `GATE_QUEUE` from `activeRouterState`; do not call
        `sdd-state` or a task-lifecycle command to rediscover them. Apply the switch below, sized to
        the classified request's blast radius (`AX_PREFLIGHT_BLAST_RADIUS_SCOPED`). Its mutating arms
        are legal here only because STEP_1 already proved or opened the owning session.

        The migration arm returns exactly one fresh post-mutation snapshot as `migrationState`; set
        `activeRouterState = migrationState`. Do not run a router refresh after that return.
        Readiness branches are routing decisions over `activeRouterState`, not mutation subflows;
        every non-migration arm retains the
        current `activeRouterState`. After a mutating branch returns, write exactly
        `<branch-id> — <what it produced>` to
        `.claude/tmp/sdd-router-preflight-journal.txt`, run branchJournal once, and require success;
        the CLI consumes the payload. Then proceed to STEP_2_ROUTE with that exact active snapshot.
        Editing `specs/.sdd-session.md` by hand or writing journal free text inline is forbidden.

        <ToolCall owner="this-step" result="branchJournal">npx gennady sdd-session log --content-file .claude/tmp/sdd-router-preflight-journal.txt</ToolCall> Run once per successfully returned mutating branch; use branchJournal before routing.

        {{> "contract/process/readiness-preflight-gate"}}
      </Action>
    </Step>
    <Step id="STEP_2_ROUTE">
      <Goal>Hand control to exactly one branch, passing SCALE down as the depth parameter.</Goal>
      <Action>
        Evaluate the LOGIC_SWITCH below and follow the first matching case. The switch keys on
        intent + scope-type only — SCALE selects depth, never a branch. Hand SCALE down via the
        session file: the branch reads `scale:` from it and, per `AX_SCALE_PROPORTIONAL_DEPTH`,
        sizes its interview depth, the number of design alternatives, and the weight of the
        verification tail to that value. For module decomposition, apply the two exact input states
        and rejection branch in `AX_HANDOFF_TO_MODULE_DECOMPOSITION`; do not infer another state.
        Every loaded branch returns `TerminalDecision = continue | pause | complete` per
        `SESSION_FILE_FORMAT`. `continue` keeps this session for the selected next link; `pause` keeps
        it for resume after approval/check/cap/blocker/operator pause. A branch may return `complete`
        only from its own terminal menu after proving no chained work remains; no intermediate route
        closes the session. When routing execute, pass the exact `executeSessionMode` produced by
        STEP_1; the owner must not infer reused/fresh from filesystem reads or extra probes.
      </Action>
    </Step>
  </ExecutionPlan>

