  <LogicSwitch>
    ```
    LOGIC_SWITCH (on sdd-state + intent + scope-type):
      - WHEN forced intent = scaffold
          -> READ_AND_USE_DIRECTIVE("ai/directives/sdd-v2/scaffold.directive.xml")
      - WHEN forced intent = reconcile
          -> READ_AND_USE_DIRECTIVE("ai/directives/sdd-v2/reconcile.directive.xml")
      - WHEN forced intent = critic
          -> READ_AND_USE_DIRECTIVE("ai/directives/sdd-v2/critic.directive.xml")
      - WHEN forced intent = execute
          -> READ_AND_USE_DIRECTIVE("ai/directives/sdd-v2/execute.directive.xml")
      - WHEN specs/README.md is absent OR intent = project-setup
          (vision / scope graph / register scope / bootstrap infra)
          -> READ_AND_USE_DIRECTIVE("ai/directives/sdd-v2/root.directive.xml")
      - WHEN intent = recover-from-code (portal present, operator names a folder or file and asks to
          recover / recreate its spec from the code that already lives there)
          -> READ_AND_USE_DIRECTIVE("ai/directives/sdd-v2/recover-from-code.directive.xml")
      - WHEN intent ∈ {new-scope, evolve-scope} AND scope-type ∈ {product, library}
          -> READ_AND_USE_DIRECTIVE("ai/directives/sdd-v2/scope.directive.xml")
      - WHEN intent ∈ {new-scope, evolve-scope} AND scope-type = infrastructure
          -> READ_AND_USE_DIRECTIVE("ai/directives/sdd-v2/infra.directive.xml")
      - WHEN intent ∈ {new-scope, evolve-scope} AND scope-type = interface
          -> READ_AND_USE_DIRECTIVE("ai/directives/sdd-v2/interface.directive.xml")
      - WHEN intent = module-decomposition AND scope-type ∈ {product, library} AND either
          (a) the scope has a valid `CHANGE_MANIFEST` plus the exact `[SESSION]` working-set entry
              `<scope-spec-path> — module-decomposition handoff — operator-approved review-state draft`, OR
          (b) the scope has no `CHANGE_MANIFEST` and its exact `[SCOPES]` row's `status` column is `done` (master)
          (`AX_HANDOFF_TO_MODULE_DECOMPOSITION`)
          -> READ_AND_USE_DIRECTIVE("ai/directives/sdd-v2/module.directive.xml")
      - WHEN intent = module-decomposition AND neither exact state above holds
          -> halt `H_SCOPE_DRAFT_NOT_OPERATOR_APPROVED`; do not load the module directive
      - WHEN intent = multi-scope (one change spans several scopes)
          -> decompose the request against the Scope Graph in dependency order per `AX_CROSS_SCOPE_CHANGE`
             (the shared / cross-cutting scope first, then its dependents); for EACH scope in that order run
             its own ordinary route (branches 3–6 of this same LOGIC_SWITCH) to completion, one scope at a
             time, with a brief check-in with the operator between scopes
      - WHEN intent = execute (a concrete Task-ID, or `next` / `pick` / `batch` / `all`, or an operator
          request to run a task or the queue)
          -> READ_AND_USE_DIRECTIVE("ai/directives/sdd-v2/execute.directive.xml")
      - DEFAULT
          -> ask the operator which intent applies (message in Russian); route only on a confirmed intent
    ```
  </LogicSwitch>
</SddRouter>
